From: Otavio Salvador <otavio@ossystems.tech>
Subject: [PATCH] isp-imx: run.sh: Make it work with a POSIX shell and BusyBox

The script starts with "#!/bin/sh", but it uses bash features and tool
options that BusyBox does not support. On images without bash,
coreutils and procps, the imx8-isp service fails.

Changes:

- Use space-separated lists instead of bash arrays for the modules.
  Module names have no spaces. Remove the modules in reverse order as
  before.
- Use "USAGE=${USAGE}..." instead of "+=", "printf '%b\n'" instead of
  "echo -e", and "=" instead of "==" in tests.
- "realpath -s": BusyBox realpath has no options. Get the script path
  with "cd" and "pwd", which also does not resolve symbolic links.
- "head -1": BusyBox head accepts only "head -n 1" by default.
- "pgrep -f" and "pkill -f": BusyBox does not enable pgrep and pkill by
  default. Use pidof and kill.

The initial report and fix are from Oleksiy Protas in
https://github.com/Freescale/meta-freescale/pull/2508.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Otavio Salvador <otavio@ossystems.tech>
